APP("birth_ready", "Birth Ready", "Labour, birth and the bag — prepared, not scared", "Parenting", ["#AD1457", "#00897B", "#F9A825"], "heart",
 "Birth Ready writes your birth preferences, packs the hospital bag, coaches your birth partner, decodes contraction timing and builds a comfort toolkit for each stage of labour.",
 "You are a warm, experienced antenatal educator and doula: practical, unbiased about birth choices, honest that plans change, and never fear-mongering.",
 "Get ready for the big day", "Where and how you hope to give birth shapes the plan.", ["Birth preferences in plain language", "Partner cheat sheets", "Contraction & when-to-go-in guidance"],
 [NAME, CH("place", "Planned birth place", ["Hospital", "Birth centre", "Home", "Not sure"]), CH("hopes", "Hoping for", ["Unmedicated", "Epidural", "Water birth", "Planned caesarean", "VBAC", "Open to anything"], multi=True), TXT("partner", "Birth partner", "Sam (husband)")],
 [T("plan", "Birth preferences", "A one-page document for your team", "📝", [LONG("wishes", "Your wishes and worries", "dim lights, delayed cord clamping, scared of forceps…"), TXT("date", "Due date", "14 March")],
    "Draft a one-page birth preferences document for the profile from: {wishes} (due {date}). Sections: a quote containing the full document in first person with headings (Environment, Pain relief, Monitoring, Second stage, Third stage, Baby's first hour, If a caesarean is needed), then a checklist of preferences to confirm with the midwife before it's final, and a callout reminding that preferences are flexible and staff will explain any deviation.", "quote, checklist, callout", "Draft it", "Writing…"),
  T("bag", "Pack the bag", "Hospital bag, split by who carries it", "🎒", [CH("season", "Season", ["Summer", "Winter", "Mild"], "Mild"), CH("stay", "Expected stay", ["Day case / home birth", "1–2 nights", "3+ nights / caesarean"], "1–2 nights")],
    "Build a hospital bag list for a {stay} stay in {season}, at the profile's birth place. Sections: a checklist split into three labelled groups — Labour bag (for the room), Postnatal bag (for after) and Baby bag — with quantities, then a kv of documents and things to prepare at home (car seat fitted, maternity notes, snacks, phone numbers), and bullets of items people pack but never use.", "checklist, kv, bullets", "Pack it", "Packing…"),
  T("partner", "Partner cheat sheet", "What to do in each stage", "🤝", [CH("stage", "Stage", ["Early labour", "Active labour", "Transition", "Pushing", "First hours after"], "Active labour")],
    "Coach the profile's birth partner for {stage} of labour, matching the profile's hopes. Sections: steps for exactly what to do and say, a table (She says / does | It probably means | You do), a quote with 3 phrases that help and 3 to avoid, and a callout on when to call the midwife or press the buzzer.", "steps, table, quote, callout", "Coach partner", "Briefing…"),
  T("contractions", "Contraction check", "Timing → what stage, when to go in", "⏱️", [LONG("timing", "Your timings", "every 7 min, lasting 45s, for 1 hour; waters intact; manageable"), TXT("distance", "Minutes to birth place", "25")],
    "Interpret these contraction timings: {timing}, with {distance} minutes to the birth place, given the profile. Sections: a callout with the likely stage and a clear Stay home / Call now / Go in now verdict using standard guidance (e.g. 3 in 10 minutes lasting 60s, waters breaking, bleeding, reduced movements, feeling pushy), bullets on what to do in the meantime, and a kv of what to tell the triage line (timings, waters colour, movements, history).", "callout, bullets, kv", "Check timing", "Timing…"),
  T("comfort", "Comfort toolkit", "Positions, breathing, TENS, water", "🌊", [CH("wants", "Work with", ["Positions & movement", "Breathing", "Water", "TENS & massage", "Everything"], "Everything")],
    "Build a comfort toolkit focused on {wants} for the profile's hopes and birth place. Sections: cards (technique, meta = stage it suits · needs kit?), steps to practise the top two at home this week, a table of pain-relief options (Option | Where available | Pros | Cons | Can still move?) so choices are informed, and a callout that changing your mind on the day is fine.", "cards, steps, table, callout", "Build toolkit", "Gathering…")], BIRTH)

